{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"symfony-rules","kind":"rule","title":"Symfony rules","description":"Standing rules for Symfony apps covering autowired services, thin controllers, Doctrine repositories and migrations, forms and validator constraints, Messenger, voters and config.","category":"conventions","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["build"],"role":["backend-engineer"],"stack":["symfony"],"requires":["none"],"output":["code"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","model_tier":"mid","level":"intermediate","depth":"specific","tags":["doctrine","autowiring","voters","messenger","form-validation"],"applies_to":["src/**/*.php","config/**","templates/**/*.twig","migrations/**"],"pairs_with":{"rules":["php-style-rules"]},"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"When you write or change code in this Symfony app:\n\n**Know the project first**\n- Check the Symfony version in `composer.json` and the bundles installed (API Platform, Messenger, Security, Doctrine). Prefer PHP attributes (`#[Route]`, `#[ORM\\Entity]`, `#[Assert\\...]`) if the project uses them, and follow the existing directory layout under `src/`.\n\n**Services and DI**\n- Rely on autowiring and autoconfiguration. Inject dependencies through the constructor (readonly promoted properties); never fetch services from the container (`$this->container->get`) or make services public to reach them.\n- Bind scalar config with `#[Autowire('%param%')]` or `services.yaml` `bind`, not by reading `$_ENV` in services.\n- Keep services stateless; per-request data does not live in service properties.\n\n**Controllers**\n- Controllers stay thin: map the request (`#[MapRequestPayload]`, forms or a DTO), call a service, return a response. No Doctrine queries or business rules inline.\n- Use `#[IsGranted]` or `denyAccessUnlessGranted` with a voter for every action on a resource. Put ownership and permission rules in voters, not in `if` checks scattered across controllers and templates.\n\n**Doctrine**\n- Put queries in repository methods with descriptive names (`findActiveForCustomer`). Use the QueryBuilder or DQL with parameters; never concatenate input into DQL or SQL.\n- Avoid N+1 queries: join and select relations you will use, and paginate list queries.\n- Change the schema only with Doctrine migrations generated by `make:migration` and reviewed before committing. Never edit a migration that has run on a shared environment.\n- Call `flush()` once per unit of work, in the service, not inside loops or entity methods. Keep entities free of service dependencies.\n\n**Validation and forms**\n- Put validation rules as constraints on DTOs or entities (`#[Assert\\NotBlank]`, `#[Assert\\Length]`), and validate with the validator or form. Do not hand-roll checks that constraints cover.\n- Keep CSRF protection on for browser forms.\n\n**Async and events**\n- Send slow or retryable work (emails, webhooks, image processing) through Messenger to an async transport, with a message class carrying ids, not entities. Handlers re-load data and are idempotent.\n- Use event subscribers for cross-cutting reactions; keep them small and do not hide core business flow in listeners.\n\n**Configuration and secrets**\n- Store secrets in the Symfony secrets vault or real environment variables, not committed `.env` files. `.env` holds non-secret defaults only; `.env.local` is never committed.\n- Production runs with `APP_ENV=prod`, `APP_DEBUG=0`, and a warmed cache.\n\n**Templates and output**\n- Rely on Twig auto-escaping; use `|raw` only for trusted, sanitised content. Generate URLs with `path()` and `url()`.\n- Use the Serializer with groups or explicit DTOs for JSON; never serialise entities wholesale.\n\n**Before you finish**\n- Run `bin/console lint:container`, PHPStan or Psalm at the project's level, and PHPUnit (including a `WebTestCase` for controllers you changed). Run `doctrine:schema:validate` after entity changes. Say what you ran.","steps":[]}
